ting protocols. PRISM is the diagnostic algebra (measures loops over time). PULSE is the temporal algebra (declares how loops cycle). OS-011 (Embodiment) is the sensorimotor behavioral protocol for "},{"id":"spn-102701","marks":["code"],"text":"&body.*"},{"id":"spn-102702","text":" providers — closes the perception-action gap by defining the typed "},{"id":"spn-102703","marks":["code"],"text":"perceive/act/affordances/encode_state/replay"},{"id":"spn-102704","text":" loop. Together with the eight cognitive primitives (OS-001 through OS-008) and the [&] structural composition layer, they form the complete protocol stack."}]},{"id":"blk-71593","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-102705","text":"Separate spec documents"}]},{"id":"blk-71594","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-71596","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102706","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/spec/OS-008-HARNESS.md"},{"id":"spn-102707","text":" — Agent Harness Protocol (pipeline enforcement, quality gates, sprint contracts, context management)"}]}],"id":"blk-71595","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-71598","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102708","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/spec/OS-009-PRISM-SPECIFICATION.md"},{"id":"spn-102709","text":" — PRISM Protocol for Rating Iterative System Memory (9 CL dimensions, 4-phase evaluation loop, BYOR, IRT calibration)"}]}],"id":"blk-71597","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-71600","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102710","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/spec/OS-010-PULSE-SPECIFICATION.md"},{"id":"spn-102711","text":" — PULSE Protocol for Uniform Loop State Exchange (loop manifest schema, 5 canonical phase kinds, 6 canonical tokens as of v0.1.1, 7 invariants, BYOL)"}]}],"id":"blk-71599","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-71602","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102712","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/spec/OS-011-EMBODIMENT.md"},{"id":"spn-102713","text":" — Embodiment Protocol (typed perceive/act/affordances/encode_state/replay loop for "},{"id":"spn-102714","marks":["code"],"text":"&body.*"},{"id":"spn-102715","text":", InteractionTrace schema, SurpriseSignal PULSE token, 5 invariants, 12 conformance tests)"}]}],"id":"blk-71601","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-71604","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102716","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/spec/OS-E001-EMPIRICAL-EVALUATION.md"},{"id":"spn-102717","text":" — Empirical Evaluation of Topology-Aware Continual Learning (Graphonomous benchmark on [&] portfolio)"}]}],"id":"blk-71603","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-71605","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-102718","text":"Relationship to other projects"}]},{"id":"blk-71606","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-71608","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102719","text":"OpenSentience defines the theoretical protocols; [&] portfolio companies implement them"}]}],"id":"blk-71607","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-71610","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102720","text":"Graphonomous implements OS-001 (continual learning) and is the canonical PULSE substrate for "},{"id":"spn-102721","marks":["code"],"text":"memory"}]}],"id":"blk-71609","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-71612","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102722","text":"AmpersandBoxDesign implements OS-002 through OS-005 as prompts and contracts"}]}],"id":"blk-71611","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-71614","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102723","text":"Delegatic implements OS-006 (governance) and is the canonical PULSE substrate for "},{"id":"spn-102724","marks":["code"],"text":"policy"},{"id":"spn-102725","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-102726","marks":["code"],"text":"audit"}]}],"id":"blk-71613","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-71616","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102727","text":"OS-008 (Harness) sits above OS-006 — enforces pipeline ordering, quality gates, and governance contracts at runtime"}]}],"id":"blk-71615","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-71618","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102728","text":"OS-009 (PRISM) lives in "},{"id":"spn-102729","marks":["code"],"text":"/home/travis/ProjectAmp2/PRISM/"},{"id":"spn-102730","text":" (Elixir codebase, Fly.io deploy)"}]}],"id":"blk-71617","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-71620","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102731","text":"OS-010 (PULSE) lives in "},{"id":"spn-102732","marks":["code"],"text":"/home/travis/ProjectAmp2/PULSE/"},{"id":"spn-102733","text":" (manifest standard + reference manifests + JSON Schema)"}]}],"id":"blk-71619","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-71622","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102734","text":"Every portfolio product declares its own loop topology via a PULSE manifest in "},{"id":"spn-102735","marks":["code"],"text":"<project>/docs/spec/README.md"},{"id":"spn-102736","text":" under the \"PULSE Loop Manifest\" section"}]}],"id":"blk-71621","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-71623","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-102737","text":"Homepage build (data-driven, anti-drift)"}]},{"id":"blk-71624","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102738","text":"The homepage ("},{"id":"spn-102739","marks":["code"],"text":"index.html"},{"id":"spn-102740","text":") is "},{"id":"spn-102741","marks":["bold"],"text":"generated"},{"id":"spn-102742","text":", not hand-edited. Source lives in "},{"id":"spn-102743","marks":["code"],"text":"_rebuild/"},{"id":"spn-102744","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-71625","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-71627","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102745","marks":["code"],"text":"_rebuild/data/{site,protocols,rungs,references}.json"},{"id":"spn-102746","text":" — single source of truth. The protocol "},{"id":"spn-102747","marks":["bold"],"text":"count"},{"id":"spn-102748","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-102749","marks":["bold"],"text":"OS-NNN range"},{"id":"spn-102750","text":" in the hero/headings are DERIVED from "},{"id":"spn-102751","marks":["code"],"text":"protocols.length"},{"id":"spn-102752","text":", never typed — so \"missing OS-011/OS-012\" or a wrong count is structurally impossible."}]}],"id":"blk-71626","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-71629","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102753","marks":["code"],"text":"_rebuild/build/templates.mjs"},{"id":"spn-102754","text":" — zero-dependency template-literal components."}]}],"id":"blk-71628","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-71631","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102755","marks":["code"],"text":"_rebuild/build/build.mjs"},{"id":"spn-102756","text":" — validates data (fails the build on drift: bad id, unknown status, missing field, out-of-order ids) then renders."}]}],"id":"blk-71630","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-71633","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102757","marks":["code"],"text":"_rebuild/styles/site.css"},{"id":"spn-102758","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-102759","marks":["code"],"text":"_rebuild/build/proof.js"},{"id":"spn-102760","text":" — design tokens + the κ proof UI; "},{"id":"spn-102761","marks":["code"],"text":"kappa_proof.js"},{"id":"spn-102762","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-102763","marks":["code"],"text":"amp-nav.js"},{"id":"spn-102764","text":" already live at the site root."}]}],"id":"blk-71632","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-71634","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-102765","text":"To change the homepage: edit the JSON/templates, run "},{"id":"spn-102766","marks":["code"],"text":"node _rebuild/build/build.mjs"},{"id":"spn-102767","text":", then copy "},{"id":"spn-102768","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/index.html"},{"id":"spn-102769","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-102770","marks":["code"],"text":"index.html"},{"id":"spn-102771","text":", "},{"id":"spn-102772","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/styles/site.css"},{"id":"spn-102773","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-102774","marks":["code"],"text":"styles/site.css"},{"id":"spn-102775","text":", "},{"id":"spn-102776","marks":["co